  "body": "**What's missing:** a tool's controller number (`SetToolNumber`, #221, `crates/app/src/commands/tool_number.rs`) can't be set or read over MCP. That number is the `T..` / `H..` a post writes, and it has to match the machine's tool table. A headless agent's tools always post as their position in the document's tool list. On `main` ed24aead, a job that adds EM-1000-4FL, EM-0600-4FL and DR-0300 posts EM-1000-4FL as `T03` (its place in the sorted list), whatever pocket it sits in on the machine. `get_job`'s tool rows don't show the number either, so the agent can't see what will be posted.\n\n**Neighbour that works:** the GUI's tool editor sets it through `SetToolNumber` (one undo step). Refused by name: an unknown or non-tool name, a number outside 1-99999, a number another tool already has, and a no-op. `tool_numbers::numbers` gives every tool the number it posts as.\n\n**Done means:**\n- A `set_tool_number { tool, number }` tool runs `SetToolNumber` through `env.history`. `number` is an integer, or `null` to go back to the list position.\n- It returns the tool's own number and the number it posts as.\n- `get_job`'s tool rows gain `number` (the tool's own, or null) and `posts_as`.\n- The command's refusals come back as tool errors.\n- In-process JSON-RPC tests pin it: a renumbered tool posts as that `T` word, undo puts the old number back, and the refusals are named.\n\nLabels per AGENTS.md for an agent-filed issue: `enhancement`, `P2`, `area:ui`, `source:agent` (this account can't set labels).\n",
